  "details": "An input overlay displays real-time thumbstick or gimbal positions on the X/Y axis, providing a direct visual link between a pilot's inputs and the drone's behavior. This overlay is an invaluable tool for new and experienced pilots.\n\nFor new pilots, it simplifies learning by making it easier to understand control inputs and seek feedback. For experienced pilots, it enables better demonstrations by making all maneuvers easier to study and reproduce. \n\nIt also helps when diagnosing input-related issues and fine-tuning control rates.\n\nIts standard in all other drone sims and would be a great addition to the drone system. \n\nAttached is the implementation from Liftoff, another popular drone simulator. Since vrchat allows users to swap the Throttle, Yaw, Pitch, and Roll axes maybe adding small labels \"T, Y, P, R\" to the axes or directional symbols might be useful. Alternatively a label to denote the control mode i.e. \"Mode: 4\"",
